ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=sh
 aroncrouch@me.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:sharoncrouch@me.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=frank@
 clintonfernandez.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:frank@clintonfernandez.com
CREATED:20240618T153159Z
DESCRIPTION:undefined\n\nKELCEY KIRCHER CHEA\nTo: Frank Fernandez (Viewed) 
 \, Sharon F Crouch (Not viewed)\nJun 17\, 2024 at 09:07:00 AM\nMessage body
 :\nKaiser Permanente Bipolar Skills Class (Online Class/Group)\n \nDear Cla
 ss Participant\,\n \nThank you for your interest in the Bipolar Skills Onli
 ne Class. Your class is scheduled from 3:30 PM to 5:00 PM on Tuesdays.\n \n
   \nYour referring provider previously asked for your consent to receive se
 cure messages through KP.org or emails at a personal address about this onl
 ine class. The virtual class will take place on a platform called MS Teams.
  This message contains instructions for joining the class via Smart Phone\,
  Computer\, or Call-in Audio Only options. Please log in 15 minutes in adva
 nce to manage any technical difficulties that may arise and ensure that you
  are ready to start group promptly at 3:30 PM. The login information in thi
 s message will help you access any class during the series. \n \nConsent fo
 r Care: \n \nBy taking the actions to join this group or class via Teams\, 
 you consent to participate in a virtual group class with a Kaiser Permanent
 e health care provider via video conferencing. If you do not consent to thi
 s form of care\, if you have any questions or if you prefer to disenroll\, 
 please call the Department at (916) 973-5300.\n \nClass Norms:\n \nFor a su
 ccessful and confidential class experience for yourself and others\, you mu
 st have a quiet\, private location where you will not be interrupted and ot
 hers (who are not participating in the class) cannot overhear the discussio
 n of the class. If you cannot be alone\, please use headphones and protect 
 any screens you are using to ensure they are not viewable by others.\n \nPl
 ease log in 15 minutes in advance to manage any technical difficulties that
  may arise and ensure that you are ready to start program promptly at the b
 eginning of the class.\n \nLog-on Instructions: \n \n*The login info for ea
 ch class session will be the same. Save this message to use as a reference 
 during your time in the class. \n*You may want to save the meeting link as 
 a Favorite in your browser and/or save or write down the Phone Conference I
 D if that is easier than accessing this message in KP.org before each sessi
 on.  \n*Please determine if you prefer to join via Smartphone or Computer a
 nd follow the below steps to join:\n \nSmartphone (Android/iPhone):\n \nYou
  are required to download the Microsoft Teams App for this group session. P
 lease do this in advance of your group visit.\nWhen you are ready to join\,
  copy and paste the link from this message in a browser of your choice. You
 r Teams App will launch: \nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3am
 eeting_YjA1NDIwZTAtZjFlNC00N2IzLWFhZTctZDQwYmM1MTQ3ZmI3%40thread.v2/0?conte
 xt=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%223f8a7bc4-e337-47a5-a0fc-0d512c0e05f1%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a
 %22adba1969-cb17-41cb-beca-577694a07129%22%7d\n \nOR\n \nClick here to join
  the meeting\n \nWhen given the option\, select “Join meeting\,” not “Sign 
 in and join.” Selecting “Join meeting” will enable you to log in to the gro
 up as a Guest. For your privacy\, please use your first name and initial of
  your last name (not your full name) and do not sign-in with your personal 
 Teams account.\nSigning in as a Guest will enable you to control how you ap
 pear in the group. Please type your first name and last initial to help you
 r instructor identify you and to protect your privacy in the group. \nSelec
 t “Join meeting.” \n \nDesktop (Windows/Mac):\n \nPlease ensure you have ei
 ther a built-in camera and microphone or attached camera and microphone. \n
 When you copy and paste the link to join\, you will be prompted to either D
 ownload the Windows App or Join on the Web instead. We highly recommend Dow
 nloading the Windows App if you are able to. Please do this in advance of t
 he group visit. Here is the link:\nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-joi
 n/19%3ameeting_YjA1NDIwZTAtZjFlNC00N2IzLWFhZTctZDQwYmM1MTQ3ZmI3%40thread.v2
 /0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%223f8a7bc4-e337-47a5-a0fc-0d512c0e05f1%22%2c%22O
 id%22%3a%22adba1969-cb17-41cb-beca-577694a07129%22%7d\n \nOR\n \nClick here
  to join the meeting\n \nWhen given the option\, select “Join meeting\,” no
 t “Sign in and join.” Selecting “Join meeting” will enable you to log in to
  the group as a Guest. For your privacy\, please use your first name and in
 itial of your last name (not your full name) and do not sign-in with your p
 ersonal Teams account.\nSigning in as a Guest will enable you to control ho
 w you appear in the group. Please type your first name and last initial to 
 help your instructor identify you and to protect your privacy in the group.
  \nSelect “Join meeting.” \n \nCall-in Audio Only Option (use if you don't 
 have access to a Smart Phone or Computer\n \nPlease note that the number yo
 u call in from will be displayed as your screen name. For your privacy\, we
  recommend dialing *67 before the audio-only number:  *67 (213) 533-9530.\n
 Enter the Phone Conference ID as follows: 886 316 974#   For the best audio
  experience\, use earbuds or a headset to reduce audio feedback.\nWhen you 
 enter *67\, your number will not appear to other attendees in the group. Th
 e instructor will take attendance by asking you for your first name and las
 t initial. This will ensure that your attendance is noted and you will rema
 in booked for remaining classes in the series.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240618T153159Z
